# Performance analysis reports (generated during runtime; keep only the
# canonical TODO-25 evidence files tracked, referenced by verify_todo25_*)
reports/p1_analyze_latency_*.json

# Performance benchmark run artifacts (regenerated by
# scripts/benchmark_performance.py; never evidence of record)
reports/performance/*.json

# P5 forward-test run logs (runtime evidence, graded by verify_p5_forward_test)
reports/p5_forward_test_*.json
# Single-writer guard sidecar (kernel lock held by the live supervisor)
reports/p5_forward_test_*.json.claim

# Archived stub-era run logs + stray runtime files (2026-09-07 P3 hygiene
# sweep; kept for forensics, not evidence of record)
reports/archived-stubs-*/
# F8-H-01 verifier dry-run stubs (2026-09-08 evidence-stream fix: check_e
# redirects the dry-run runner here instead of the live reports/ stream).
# The verifier's own JSON result joined the same path in the F8-C-01 wave 2:
# per-run mutable output is ignored; the dated audit-history records are the
# evidence of record (same pattern as health-*.json vs health-final-*.json).
reports/health/p5-verify-stubs/
# Quarantine tables + pre-move safety copies + move manifests (2026-09-09
# benchmark test-to-production leakage remediation): the quarantine tables
# live INSIDE the sqlite DB (data/loats.db); only the safety copy and the
# manifest land on disk. Machine-local remediation state, not evidence of
# record -- the manifest is regenerated by re-running the move script.
reports/quarantine/

# Health check intermediate run artifacts (keep health-final-*.json only)
reports/health/health-fast-*.json
reports/health/health-full-*.json
reports/health/health-*.json
!reports/health/health-final-*.json
reports/health/bandit.json
reports/health/coverage.json
reports/health/fast-fixes.json
# Both spellings: the health runner writes pip_audit.json (underscore); ad-hoc
# manual pip-audit runs use the security-dir spelling pip-audit.json. The
# hyphenated variant leaked into reports/health/ on 08Sep — ignore both.
reports/health/pip_audit.json
reports/health/pip-audit.json
reports/health/run*.json
reports/health/only-probes.json

# F8-H-03 runtime verification report (generated artifact, external verifier emits
# reports/f8-h-03-verification.json; keep it out of the index)
reports/*.json

# Canonical P1 evidence of record (negations must sit AFTER reports/*.json —
# git honours the last matching rule). 20260904_040609 is the F8-L-03
# discharge artifact (100/100 live TCS round trips, live-endpoint scope) so
# HC-29 passes from a fresh clone. (The 20260828_084822 pre-sweep baseline
# was dropped on the 06Sep merge to keep the merged tree at the 383 ceiling;
# the 04Sep run supersedes it.)
!reports/p1_analyze_latency_20260904_040609.json

# Security-scan run artifacts under reports/security/ (2026-09-06): bandit,
# safety and pip-audit JSON emitted per invocation are re-derivable and
# embed machine-absolute paths; the evidence of record is the dated snapshot
# scheme (bandit-20260901.json, pip-audit-20260901.json). CI's
# security.yml writes its own root-level copies (below).
reports/security/bandit.json
reports/security/safety-report.json
reports/security/pip-audit.json

# Junk files
$null
[100%]
0.21.0
pytest_final*.log
bandit-report.json
pip-audit-core-report.json
pip-audit-report.json
